example.after:
// Separated modules
// monitor.rs - handles monitoring logic only
// validator.rs - handles validation
// persistence.rs - handles data storage
// ui.rs - handles user interface

// Interface boundary
// Daemon depends on Monitor trait
// Monitor implements Monitor trait
// Modules communicate through defined interface

// Repository pattern
// EntropyCalculator depends on StorageRepository trait
// DiskStorage implements StorageRepository
// MemoryStorage implements StorageRepository for testing

// Event-driven architecture
// Monitor emits events (BatteryChanged, FocusStateChanged)
// UI subscribes to events
// Modules are decoupled

// Layered architecture
// Presentation layer - handles UI and user interaction
// Business logic layer - implements rules and calculations
// Data access layer - handles storage and retrieval
// Dependencies flow inward

// Dependency injection
// Monitor receives Storage through constructor
// Enables testing with mock implementations
// Improves flexibility
